markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Foundations of AI Programming Curriculum Overview

The **Foundations of AI Programming** curriculum unit introduces students to web app development, JavaScript programming, and user-centered design.

They learn how to plan, build, and style a web app, how to use AI as a coding partner, and how JavaScript brings a page to life through events, variables, functions, and logic.

<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div>
    <div><h2>Students will:</h2></div>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt">
      <li>Design and structure a web app, using layout patterns that guide how users think and move through a page.</li><br>
      <li>Use CSS and the POUR principles to style a page and make it usable for everyone.</li><br>
      <li>Use JavaScript event listeners and handlers to make a web app respond to user actions through the DOM.</li><br>
      <li>Use variables, conditionals, loops, and functions to create, test, and refine a working program.</li><br>
      <li>Evaluate AI-generated code for correctness and fit, rather than accepting it by default.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

</div>

---

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

## Unit Calendar 

Take a quick look at the lessons included in this unit using the calendar tool.

This version of the calendar assumes 5 lessons per week and can be customized using the drop-down menu to accommodate your schedule. 

Check out the <a href="https://studio.code.org/s/aif1-2026" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">calendar feature</a> on top of the unit preview. 

